    "result_text": "All 260 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures, 0 errors. (The stack trace in the earlier log was from `createUserNoRolesFails`, a test that intentionally logs an expected failure path \u2014 it passed.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) across the application:\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` response property (string, `GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) with `membershipLevel`, an `integer` (int32) constrained to `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`, `readOnly`. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with `getMembershipLevel`/`setMembershipLevel` and drops `membershipTier`.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced `formatMembershipTier` (returning `String`) with `formatMembershipLevel` (returning `Integer`): starts at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure). Updated the `@Mapping` to target `membershipLevel`.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 \n- Removed the now-obsolete `membershipTier(Owner)` helper (the GOLD/household override), since level depends only on email and namesake count and is derived entirely by the mapper.\n- Removed the two `ownerDto.setMembershipTier(...)` calls in `getOwner` and `addOwner`; the mapper populates `membershipLevel` automatically.\n- Updated the create audit line to record `membershipLevel` instead of the tier.\n\nThe new acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` (level 3 for an owner with email + unique name) passes, along with all existing tests.",
